+\subsection{Primary ideals and finite contact algebras}
+Theorem~\ref{thm:quartic-primary} identifies the actual ideal as
+$\mathcal I_{S_4}\cap\mathcal I_{C_4}^{m(m+1)/2}$, and gives
+all its infinitesimal layers. The secant cubic and the conic
+$AC-B^2$ are classical; the claimed multiplication statement is
+the precise thickening exponent and ideal equality. Its proof
+uses Lemma~\ref{lem:weighted-relation-minors}, not a generic
+matrix normal form. Theorem~\ref{thm:contact-pencil-primary}
+concerns a different, explicitly described Grassmannian family.
+Its power-basis determinant is proved directly by confluent
+interpolation. The assertion requiring comparison is the
+conductor-induced equality with the original multiplication ideal,
+together with the complete primary decomposition and degree wall.
+Neither result asserts a primary decomposition for arbitrary
+quadratic excess components or for all higher-product subseries.
+The first-page information about \cite{Ballico93} cannot settle
+the priority of either assertion; that source comparison remains
+an explicit scholarly obligation.
+
